  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets a 7% interim cap for 24 months then 5%, but has no sales-stop, so a model above the limit can keep being sold while under corrective action, which mainly benefits Northwind's Hearth 10. Customers receive complete per-model 55 °C results before purchase, while the public is barred from seeing individual-company rates, and S5 keeps the 8-per-100k mandatory recall with no transition, which weighs on Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S3 gives a 6-year retrofit window that suits Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage, and S4's 36-month lead time meets Halcyon's red line."
